    try (Connection c = ds.getConnection();
         Statement st = c.createStatement();
         ResultSet rs = st.executeQuery(
             "SELECT name, tagline, price_cents, badge FROM plans WHERE active = true ORDER BY sort_order")) {
        while (rs.next()) {
            String name = rs.getString("name");
            String slug = NON_SLUG.matcher(name.toLowerCase()).replaceAll("-");
            String price = money.format(rs.getLong("price_cents") / 100.0);

            html.append("<article class=\"plan\" id=\"plan-").append(slug).append("\">");
            html.append("<h3>").append(name).append("</h3>");
            html.append("<p class=\"tagline\">").append(rs.getString("tagline")).append("</p>");
            html.append("<p class=\"price\">").append(price).append("</p>");
            String badge = rs.getString("badge");
            if (badge != null) {
                html.append("<span class=\"badge\">").append(badge).append("</span>");
            }
            html.append("</article>");
        }
    }
    return html.toString();
}
```

**Green Notes**
- **Named columns instead of `SELECT *`** (reduces E, network): the loop reads only four columns. `SELECT *` also pulls every other column of `plans` from the database on every page view. If the table has large columns such as long descriptions or terms HTML, those bytes were fetched and thrown away. [Reduce transmitted data](https://patterns.greensoftware.foundation/development/data-handling/reduce-transmitted-data)
- **Hoisted loop invariants** (reduces E): `Pattern.compile` ran once per plan row, and the pattern never changes, so it is now a `static final`. The `NumberFormat` and `Locale` depend only on `lang`, so they are built once per call.
